From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:28:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 51/89] render: particle operators run the way Wallpaper
 Engine's interpreter does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485's operator interpreter (GH 0x140265800, a byte-code loop over
4-wide particle arrays; record layouts from the parser GH 0x1401f3120's stores):

- Every step, size, alpha and colour go back to their spawn values and each operator multiplies
  them: alphafade × alphachange × oscillatealpha compose (alphachange overwrote alphafade).
- movement / angularmovement: v' = v + g·dt, p += v'·dt, v = v'·(1 − min (drag·fdt, 0.9999999)).
  Gravity and force carry the speed override; the rotation step no longer does (spin had it twice).
- fdt, the forces' step, is dt · min (0.025 / frame time, 1)^0.7 (GH 0x14025c2e0). The frame time
  is inferred to be the real one.
- sizechange / alphachange / colorchange: a clamped life ramp, multiplying. sizechange's start and
  end values carry the size override (patch op 7), so a system with it takes the override twice.
  colorchange's values are colorn-shifted like colorrandom's.
- oscillatealpha / oscillatesize: f = fmin + r·Δf, φ = pmin + r·Δp,
  value ×= smin + Δs·r·(sin (f·(age + φ)) + 1) / 2, with one random r per particle (WE keeps one,
  drawn at spawn).
- oscillateposition: the offset s·sin (f·(age + φ)) applied as a per-step difference; y's phase is
  φ + 2πr, z reuses x's. The speed override scales the frequency.
- controlpointattract: reads `offset` (not `origin`) and the full threshold (LWE halved it);
  step = scale·fdt·(1 − d / threshold), never past the point with flags bit 1; flags bit 0 kills
  particles within deletethreshold.
- vortex: v += (r̂ × axis)·(speedinner + t·Δspeed)·fdt, t clamped between distanceinner and outer.
  Plain vortex reads only flags bit 0; the ring and centre-force bits are vortex_v2's (kept as
  LWE's model, unverified: no library scene uses vortex_v2).
- turbulence: per masked axis a scalar 3D simplex noise of (position + r·Δphase + time·timescale)
  ·scale, with permuted coordinates per axis, × (speedmin + r·Δspeed)·mask·fdt. It was a
  normalised curl with one phase and speed per operator. timescale carries the rate override. The
  noise is a standard simplex: WE's own gradient hash (GH 0x14012c280) isn't ported.
- Override bindings (P15): speed into emitter speeds, velocity/angular/turbulent velocity and
  mapsequence, not into rotationrandom; size into sizerandom; lifetime into lifetimerandom; each
  skipped when the particle flags have 0x10 / 0x80 / 0x40.
- boxrandom's speedmin/speedmax give a velocity outward from the box's centre (GH 0x14025cfe0;
  box particles started at rest).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B11 (P15, P22, P28, P31, P32, P33)
